1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,574
To check a tyre's pressure,
you must let a little air out.

2
00:00:03,974 --> 00:00:08,668
Dip a big thermometer into one tiny
drop of hot water, and the drop cools

3
00:00:08,668 --> 00:00:09,568
down.

4
00:00:09,227 --> 00:00:11,474
Measuring something can change it.

5
00:00:11,874 --> 00:00:13,849
Aarav saw it at the cycle shop.

6
00:00:13,849 --> 00:00:16,962
The gauge hissed, and the
tyre got a little softer.

7
00:00:17,312 --> 00:00:20,168
For an electron, this
problem is not small.

8
00:00:20,168 --> 00:00:21,749
It is the whole story.

9
00:00:22,249 --> 00:00:26,585
By the end of this video, you will
see why nobody can draw the exact path

10
00:00:26,585 --> 00:00:27,660
of an electron.

11
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:32,784
In nineteen twenty seven, Werner
Heisenberg stated a rule of nature.

12
00:00:33,134 --> 00:00:37,522
It is impossible to know both the
exact position and the exact momentum

13
00:00:37,522 --> 00:00:39,795
of an electron at the same time.

14
00:00:40,195 --> 00:00:42,144
Position means where it is.

15
00:00:42,144 --> 00:00:45,620
Momentum is mass times
velocity, how it is moving.

16
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:49,941
The more exactly you know one, the
less exactly you can know the other.

17
00:00:50,541 --> 00:00:52,815
Let's see why, on our molecule bench.

18
00:00:52,815 --> 00:00:55,689
To see an electron, we
must hit it with light.

19
00:00:56,039 --> 00:00:58,542
First, light of a long wavelength.

20
00:00:58,542 --> 00:01:00,141
Its photon is gentle.

21
00:01:00,141 --> 00:01:02,000
The electron barely moves.

22
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:05,079
But a long wave gives a blurry picture.

23
00:01:05,079 --> 00:01:08,268
The electron could be
anywhere in this wide box.

24
00:01:08,268 --> 00:01:09,797
Position is uncertain.

25
00:01:10,197 --> 00:01:13,448
Now use a very short
wavelength, to pin it down.

26
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:14,641
The box shrinks.

27
00:01:14,641 --> 00:01:16,398
Now we know where it is.

28
00:01:16,798 --> 00:01:21,243
But a short wavelength photon
carries big momentum, h over lambda.

29
00:01:21,243 --> 00:01:24,843
It kicks the electron hard,
in an unknown direction.

30
00:01:24,843 --> 00:01:26,957
Now its momentum is uncertain.

31
00:01:27,607 --> 00:01:28,882
Look at the chart.

32
00:01:28,882 --> 00:01:31,797
Squeeze one side, and
the other side stretches.

33
00:01:31,797 --> 00:01:34,539
The area can never drop
below a fixed limit.

34
00:01:35,189 --> 00:01:37,756
Let's write it down, one step at a time.

35
00:01:38,106 --> 00:01:39,049
Step one.

36
00:01:39,049 --> 00:01:42,063
Delta x is the uncertainty in position.

37
00:01:42,063 --> 00:01:45,076
Delta p is the uncertainty in momentum.

38
00:01:45,826 --> 00:01:46,751
Step two.

39
00:01:46,751 --> 00:01:50,878
Their product can never be
smaller than h over four pi.

40
00:01:50,878 --> 00:01:55,839
Delta x times delta p is greater
than or equal to h over four pi.

41
00:01:56,589 --> 00:01:57,722
Step three.

42
00:01:57,722 --> 00:01:59,311
Momentum is m v.

43
00:01:59,311 --> 00:02:03,981
So delta x times delta v is
at least h over four pi m.

44
00:02:04,731 --> 00:02:05,631
Step four.

45
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:07,492
Notice the m at the bottom.

46
00:02:07,492 --> 00:02:10,000
A bigger mass makes the limit smaller.

47
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:13,162
So compare two objects side by side.

48
00:02:13,162 --> 00:02:16,023
A grain of one milligram, and an electron.

49
00:02:16,423 --> 00:02:21,212
For the milligram grain, h over four
pi m is about ten to the minus twenty

50
00:02:21,212 --> 00:02:22,112
eight.

51
00:02:21,819 --> 00:02:23,561
Far too small to matter.

52
00:02:23,961 --> 00:02:27,177
For the electron, it is
about ten to the minus four.

53
00:02:27,177 --> 00:02:29,199
Huge, at the scale of an atom.

54
00:02:29,599 --> 00:02:30,751
Pause and think.

55
00:02:30,751 --> 00:02:34,789
Does the uncertainty principle stop
us from tracking a cricket ball?

56
00:02:37,989 --> 00:02:38,889
No!

57
00:02:38,479 --> 00:02:41,621
Its mass is so big that the limit is tiny.

58
00:02:41,621 --> 00:02:46,095
The principle matters only for very
small particles like electrons.

59
00:02:46,745 --> 00:02:47,872
Remember this.

60
00:02:47,872 --> 00:02:51,241
An electron has no exact
path that we can know.

61
00:02:51,241 --> 00:02:52,631
Only probabilities.

62
00:02:53,331 --> 00:02:55,066
Now, one worked example.

63
00:02:55,366 --> 00:02:59,941
We locate an electron to within one
times ten to the minus ten metres.

64
00:02:59,941 --> 00:03:02,363
That is about the size of an atom.

65
00:03:02,863 --> 00:03:06,068
What is the smallest
uncertainty in its velocity?

66
00:03:06,568 --> 00:03:10,918
Delta v is h over four pi,
times m, times delta x.

67
00:03:11,668 --> 00:03:16,339
The bottom is four pi, times nine
point one zero nine times ten to the

68
00:03:16,339 --> 00:03:19,562
minus thirty one, times
ten to the minus ten.

69
00:03:19,562 --> 00:03:24,120
That is one point one four five
times ten to the minus thirty nine.

70
00:03:24,870 --> 00:03:30,155
Six point six two six times ten to the
minus thirty four, divided by that,

71
00:03:30,155 --> 00:03:34,819
is five point seven nine times
ten to the five metres per second.

72
00:03:35,569 --> 00:03:37,232
That uncertainty is huge.

73
00:03:37,232 --> 00:03:40,386
So we cannot say where
the electron will be next.

74
00:03:40,386 --> 00:03:43,578
A fixed orbit, like Bohr
drew, cannot be right.

75
00:03:44,228 --> 00:03:46,540
This is why Bohr's model had to go.

76
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:51,336
It gave the electron an exact circle,
with an exact speed, at every moment.

77
00:03:51,736 --> 00:03:55,241
The uncertainty principle says
no such path can be known.

78
00:03:55,241 --> 00:04:00,015
In its place, we can only talk about
the probability of finding the electron.

79
00:04:00,665 --> 00:04:02,130
Now, the exam trap.

80
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:06,617
Many students think the uncertainty
comes from bad instruments, so better

81
00:04:06,617 --> 00:04:08,231
machines could remove it.

82
00:04:08,631 --> 00:04:09,531
Wrong.

83
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,099
It is a law of nature.

84
00:04:11,099 --> 00:04:14,823
Even a perfect instrument
cannot beat h over four pi.

85
00:04:15,473 --> 00:04:17,155
Where is this asked?

86
00:04:17,155 --> 00:04:22,266
As numericals on delta x times delta
p, and as ratio questions comparing

87
00:04:22,266 --> 00:04:23,180
particles.

88
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:25,042
Exam level now.

89
00:04:25,042 --> 00:04:30,158
An electron and a proton are located
with the same uncertainty in position.

90
00:04:30,158 --> 00:04:35,048
What is the ratio of the minimum
uncertainty in their velocities, electron

91
00:04:35,048 --> 00:04:35,979
to proton?

92
00:04:35,979 --> 00:04:39,714
The proton is about eighteen
thirty six times heavier.

93
00:04:39,714 --> 00:04:41,030
Pause and solve.

94
00:04:46,430 --> 00:04:47,686
The answer is C.

95
00:04:47,686 --> 00:04:49,428
About eighteen thirty six.

96
00:04:49,928 --> 00:04:53,953
Delta v is at least h
over four pi m delta x.

97
00:04:54,453 --> 00:04:57,961
Same delta x, so delta
v goes as one over m.

98
00:04:58,461 --> 00:05:02,835
The ratio is the proton's mass over
the electron's, about eighteen thirty

99
00:05:02,835 --> 00:05:03,735
six.

100
00:05:03,339 --> 00:05:07,109
B, forty three, takes a
square root that is not there.

101
00:05:07,709 --> 00:05:09,166
Here is your recap.

102
00:05:09,166 --> 00:05:10,663
Screenshot this card.

103
00:05:13,863 --> 00:05:16,699
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

104
00:05:17,099 --> 00:05:17,999
One.

105
00:05:17,594 --> 00:05:21,622
Write the uncertainty principle,
and say what each symbol means.

106
00:05:22,422 --> 00:05:23,322
Two.

107
00:05:22,898 --> 00:05:25,594
Why does it not matter for a cricket ball?

108
00:05:26,394 --> 00:05:27,294
Three.

109
00:05:27,022 --> 00:05:30,302
Why does it rule out fixed
orbits for electrons?

110
00:05:31,202 --> 00:05:35,780
Next time: if an electron has no
path, how do we describe it at all?

111
00:05:35,780 --> 00:05:38,604
We find out in the
quantum mechanical model.
